                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 0,
                "retweet_count": 0,
                "source": "Twitter Web Client",
                "text": "I hosted a roundtable discussion in Chico with the Federal Home Loan Bank of San Francisco and local banks, developers, and housing advocates to address the need to build additional housing and particularly the affordable housing crisis. Economic challenges, high insurance costs, and wildfires have made it important for us to come together and find real-world solutions. We explored how public-private partnerships and regulatory reforms can help increase housing supply and affordability, and I appreciate everyone who participated for their insights and dedication.\n\nThe Chico Housing Action Team has received $100,000 in grant funding through the FHL Bank\u2019s AHEAD program to enhance its efforts in supporting those seeking affordable housing. FHLSF has also given over $750,000 to middle-income residents of our district for down payment assistance. Together, we can create opportunities that protect our way of life and stimulate our local economy.",
