                "reply_count": 36,
                "retweet_count": 6,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "Today, the House passed their budget resolution for fiscal year 2025. This budget resolution is a critical step toward restoring fiscal responsibility and reining in Washington\u2019s out-of-control spending, and does not include any mention of cuts to Medicare, Medicaid, Social Security, or SNAP.\n\nBy moving toward a balanced budget, we can put money back into the pockets of Americans instead of fueling more debt and inflation. It\u2019s time to prioritize policies that grow the economy, cut waste, prevent unnecessary tax hikes, and ensure a stronger financial future for the American people. I look forward to the next steps in the reconciliation process to build on this progress and deliver results.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
