                "reply_count": 8,
                "retweet_count": 0,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "Today, I introduced the Rural Hospital Fairness Act to legislatively fix a major mistake made by the Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services (CMS) that cost Glenn Medical Center its Critical Access Hospital status earlier this year.\n\nGlenn Medical did everything right. For more than twenty years, it served patients, followed the rules, and maintained its designation with CMS approval. Then CMS suddenly decided to change how they measure distance between hospitals \u2014 using rural backroads instead of main highways \u2014 and took Glenn Medical\u2019s status away. Now, even CMS admits it was their error from over 20 years ago, but instead of fixing it, they\u2019re letting Glenn County pay the price.\n\nMy bill will direct CMS to restore Critical Access status for hospitals like Glenn Medical that were properly designated before 2002 and still meet the intent of the law. This is about fairness and accountability. Rural hospitals shouldn\u2019t lose vital funding because of bureaucratic mismanagement and mistakes. https://t.co/WGj38jq28W",
